Also copilot's explanation of everything (and mine own):
What direct generation does

Loads a local GGUF model and loops over each query (01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb:7, 01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb:35).

Sends one prompt that asks for relevant Swiss citations directly from the question (prompts.py:14).

Parses model text with citation regex rules (BGE, Art., law abbreviations), deduplicates, and writes predicted_citations (01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb:287, 01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb:384).

In this notebook, if no citation is found it can emit a single-space placeholder for that row (01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb:381).

(What is a GGUF: Package that contains information like weights and metadata about local LLM)

What agentic retrieval does

Builds or loads BM25 indices for two corpora: federal laws and court decisions (02_agentic_retrieval_baseline.ipynb:13, bm25_index.py:11).

(What is BM25: ranks documents that are most relevant to query)

Creates tool interfaces search_laws and search_courts that return formatted hits with excerpts (tools.py:10, tools.py:107).

Runs a ReAct loop per query:
LLM emits Thought/Action/Action Input
code parses actions
tool calls execute searches
observations are fed back for more steps
citations are collected and deduplicated
(02_agentic_retrieval_baseline.ipynb:778, 02_agentic_retrieval_baseline.ipynb:1026, prompts.py:66).
Writes semicolon-joined citations to submission (02_agentic_retrieval_baseline.ipynb:1287).

How to get direct baseline scoring on val for day 1:

Install and activate env

In PowerShell from repo root, create/activate venv and install requirements.
Make sure you can import llama_cpp (or the notebook will run in mock mode and the score is not meaningful).
Confirm validation data exists
You need val.csv in your data folder with query_id, query, and gold_citations.
The notebook reads data mode from 01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb:35.

Put a GGUF model where notebook expects it

Default model path/config is in 01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb:58.
If model is missing, it falls back to mock mode as shown in 01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb:126.

Run direct baseline notebook on val

Open 01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb.
Set DATASET_MODE to val.
Run all cells.
It writes output to submission.csv (under OUTPUT_PATH) in 01_direct_generation_baseline.ipynb:439.

Validate submission format

Run:
python validate_submission.py output/submission.csv
Validator file is validate_submission.py.
Score on validation split
Run:
python evaluate_submission.py output/submission.csv --split val
Scorer script is evaluate_submission.py.

What success looks like
Validator says PASSED.
Evaluation script prints a numeric score.
